Subject: [PATCH] net_tcp: Backport receive-path fixes (reassembly, window updates)

Two problems in KOS v2.2.1's TCP receive path, found streaming audio both ways
over the Broadband Adapter (in Flycast):

1. Out-of-order segments were accepted anywhere in the window but appended to
   the receive buffer as if in order, corrupting the stream after any lost
   frame. Backports upstream's reassembly: 5cbfe5fd ("net: Add out-of-order
   TCP segment reassembly") and f4c0b536 ("net: Duplicate OOO segments are now
   rejected"). Upstream's delayed-ACK counter (ack_pending) comes with it.
2. Reading data never told the sender that the window had reopened, so after
   the window filled the sender waited for its zero-window probes: downloads
   crawled at a few KB/s. Same idea as upstream d7f97230 ("net_tcp: Send a
   window-update ACK when the receive window reopens"), adapted, since its
   base is not in v2.2.1: ACK when a read reopens the window from zero or by an
   MSS, or when an ACK is pending.
---
--- a/kernel/net/net_tcp.c
+++ b/kernel/net/net_tcp.c
@@ -133,6 +133,14 @@
